4. Imported Kernel Source and Other Components

4.1 Imported Rockchip Linux kernel source

The Rockchip kernel drivers and support code under common/kernel/files are
derived from the Rockchip Linux 6.1 kernel line previously carried by this
SDK. The corresponding public source family is:

  https://github.com/rockchip-linux/kernel
  branch: develop-6.1

The imported files retain their original headers and carry local Linux 7.3
compatibility and RK3566 integration changes.

RK628 HDMI-to-MIPI CSI-2 bridge
  Imported paths:
    common/kernel/files/drivers/media/i2c/rk628/
    common/kernel/files/drivers/media/i2c/rk628/include/

  Copyright holders identified in the source:
    Copyright (c) 2016-2023 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
    Copyright (c) 2016 Fuzhou Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
    Authors include Shunqing Chen and Dingxian Wen.
    The imported v4l2-controls_rockchip.h also retains
    Copyright (C) 2015 Intel Mobile Communications GmbH.
    The copyright header in each file controls.

  License:
    GPL-2.0, as identified by the SPDX headers.
    Certain UAPI headers are alternatively licensed under
    "GPL-2.0+ WITH Linux-syscall-note OR MIT" as stated in those files.

RKNPU driver
  Imported paths:
    common/kernel/files/drivers/rknpu/

  Copyright:
    Copyright (c) Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd.
    Authors include Felix Zeng and Finley Xiao.

  License:
    GPL-2.0, as identified by the SPDX headers.

Rockchip platform support
  Imported paths:
    common/kernel/files/drivers/firmware/rockchip_sip.c
    common/kernel/files/drivers/soc/rockchip/
    common/kernel/files/include/

  Copyright:
